From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SR7420 porting work <local@sr7420.invalid>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] backports: use native SOCKWQ flags on Linux 6.18

Linux 6.18 exposes SOCKWQ_ASYNC_NOSPACE and SOCKWQ_ASYNC_WAITDATA as
enum values in linux/net.h.  The backport header used a preprocessor
ifndef test, which cannot detect enum constants and therefore defined
aliases to the removed SOCK_ASYNC_* names.  Keep the native names and
avoid redefining them.

---
 backport-include/linux/net.h | 8 --------
 1 file changed, 8 deletions(-)

--- a/backport-include/linux/net.h
+++ b/backport-include/linux/net.h
@@ -4,12 +4,4 @@
 #include_next <linux/net.h>
 #include <linux/static_key.h>
 
-
-#ifndef SOCKWQ_ASYNC_NOSPACE
-#define SOCKWQ_ASYNC_NOSPACE   SOCK_ASYNC_NOSPACE
-#endif
-#ifndef SOCKWQ_ASYNC_WAITDATA
-#define SOCKWQ_ASYNC_WAITDATA   SOCK_ASYNC_WAITDATA
-#endif
-
 #endif /* __BACKPORT_LINUX_NET_H */
